usage: c500_benchmark.py [-h] [--control CONTROL] [--candidate CANDIDATE]
                         [--cases CASES] [--seed SEED]
                         [--lengths {full,random,boundary}] [--warmup WARMUP]
                         [--iterations ITERATIONS] [--rounds ROUNDS]
                         [--skip-correctness]

Interleaved local C500 A/B benchmark for paged-KV decode candidates. Each
round measures a control and candidate back-to-back on identical tensors,
alternating their order to avoid a one-sided clock/power bias. It reports the
per-round candidate/control ratio distribution; conclusions should use the
ratio rather than separately collected absolute timings. Examples: python
tests/c500_benchmark.py --control build/cuda_112302_control.so \ --candidate
build/cuda_maca_optimized.so --cases 7,9,12,13

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --control CONTROL
  --candidate CANDIDATE
  --cases CASES
  --seed SEED
  --lengths {full,random,boundary}
                        cache_seqlens distribution used for both control and
                        candidate
  --warmup WARMUP
  --iterations ITERATIONS
  --rounds ROUNDS
  --skip-correctness    timing-only mode for deliberately invalid phase-
                        ablation probes; never use this option as candidate
                        validation
help_exit=0
